  "question": {
    "text": "The point on the ellipse <math><mn>16</mn><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>400</mn><mo>,</mo></math> where the ordinate decreases at the same rate at which the abscissa increases is <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math> then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>b</mi></math> can be"
